{"text": "Kaiali\u2018i Kahele\n\nEXPERIENCE\nAdjunct Faculty Member, University of Hawai\u2018i (UH)-Hilo, 2014\nCollege of Agriculture, Forestry and Natural Resource Management\nHawai\u2018i Air National Guard Instructor Pilot in the 2006\nC-17 Globemaster III, 204th Airlift Squadron\nCommercial Airline Pilot, Hawaiian Airlines 2009\nAircraft Experience in the following aircrafts: 2009\nT-37; T-38; T-38C; F15C; C-130H; C-17A; B-717; B-767; A-330\nUnited States Air Force (USAF) Active Duty, Since 2004\nCombat missions flown in Afghanistan and Iraq\nMajor, USAF Field Grade Officer 2001\nHead Coach, University Laboratory School\u2019s September 1997\nVarsity Volleyball Team\nCOMMUNITY SERVICE\nSpeaker, Ellison Onizuka Day, UH-Hilo January 2016\nEmcee, Ellison Onizuka Day, UH-Hilo January 2015\nKeynote Speaker, Pacific Astronomy Engineering Summit June 2015\nCrew member, Polynesian Voyaging Society, Hikianalia 2015\nEmcee, Hawai \u2018i Island Honors Association April 2015\nKeynote Speaker, Astronaut Lacy Veach Day, November 2014\nPunahou School\nDelegate, Democratic Party, Hawai'i County Convention 2014, 2012\nDelegate, Democratic Party, State Convention, 2014, 2012\nPrecinct President, Democratic Party, District 2; Precinct 5 2014\nExecutive Director, Pa\u2018a Pono Miloli\u2018i (Hawai\u2018i Island non-profit) January 2011\nMember, Governor Neil Abercrombie appointee to July 2011\n\nExploratory Committee to consider the establishment of an\nInternational Aviation Center at Hilo International Airport and\nAdvanced Aviation Degree Training Program at UH-Hilo\n\nMost Inspirational Player Award, UH-Manoa Men\u2019s Volleyball May 1997\nKeynote Speaker, Hilo High School Commencement Exercise May 1997\nMember, Democratic Party of Hawai\u2018i Since 1992\n\nPage 1 of 2 (2/12/16)",
